    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If SceneKit reports an error when creating or loading from a scene source, the [`userInfo`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/NSError/userInfo) dictionary of the returned [`NSError`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/NSError) object may contain this key, whose value is an array of dictionaries (each containing one or more of the keys listed in [`Scene File Consistency Error Keys`](scene-file-consistency-error-keys.md)) providing details about the location of the error in the scene file.",
      "normalizedSource": "If SceneKit reports an error when creating or loading from a scene source, the [`userInfo`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/NSError/userInfo) dictionary of the returned [`NSError`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/NSError) object may contain this key, whose value is an array of dictionaries (each containing one or more of the keys listed in [`Scene File Consistency Error Keys`](scene-file-consistency-error-keys.md)) providing details about the location of the error in the scene file.",
      "sourceHash": "44adcf10ba3699f89348e468e395854a61106c50642ee4af4200bdbab8f2670d",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "If you specify [`true`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/true) for the [`checkConsistency`](scnscenesource/loadingoption/checkconsistency.md) option when creating or loading from a scene source, SceneKit verifies the scene file against the specification for its file format.",
